    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Pathological features of well-differentiated papillary mesothelial tumour of the pleura and its differential diagnosis</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Kelly J. Butnor",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Feature</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.7pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Well-differentiated papillary mesothelial tumour</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.7pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Reactive pleuritis with mesothelial hyperplasia</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.75pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Diffuse epithelioid mesothelioma with papillary pattern</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Macroscopic appearance</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Single arborescent mass or small multifocal nodules</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Masses/expansile nodules absent; may have accompanying effusion, overlying exudate, and/or adhesions</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Diffuse rind-like pleural thickening or coalescent nodular masses</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Histological growth pattern</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Surface growth</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Surface involvement &plusmn;&nbsp;overlying fibrin and associated granulation tissue featuring capillaries oriented perpendicular to surface</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Surface papillary proliferation with underlying complex/haphazard expansile growth</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Papillae </strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Range from relatively thin to broad with paucicellular myxoid or fibrovascular cores &plusmn;&nbsp;foamy macrophages</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Uncommon; stubby with simple architecture</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Architecturally complex</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Mesothelial cell morphology</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Bland monotonous monolayer</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Reactive atypia &plusmn;&nbsp;nucleolar prominence</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Cellular stratification/multilayering &plusmn;&nbsp;cytological atypia, can be deceptively bland</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Inflammation</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Rare to absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Usually present and often prominent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">If present, usually at interface of tumour with adipose tissue</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Mitoses</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Rare to absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">May be abundant (not atypical)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Relatively few, but atypical forms may be seen</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Stromal invasion</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.7pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.7pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 203.75pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"272\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Present and typically deep into submesothelial connective tissue or beyond</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 37830,
    "bookid": 35,
    "chapterId": 116,
    "fileId": 13890,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "Well-differentiated papillary mesothelial tumor (WDPMT)",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Tumour from the left visceral pleura of a 42-year-old man. Arborescent fibrovascular to myxoid papillary formations arising from the pleural surface are covered by a single layer of bland mesothelial cells with no stromal invasion.</p>",
